VeridianOS: fix compiler warnings in the KWayland client library

GCC reported, in src/client:

- -Wsubobject-linkage (buffer_p.h, surface_p.h): Buffer::Private and
  Surface::Private hold WaylandPointer<wl_buffer, wl_buffer_destroy> and
  WaylandPointer<wl_surface, wl_surface_destroy>. Those destroy functions are
  static inline in the generated wayland-client-protocol.h, so the template
  instantiations have internal linkage, while the classes live in headers
  shared by several translation units (buffer.cpp/shm_pool.cpp,
  surface.cpp/surface_p.cpp). The deleters are now destroyWlBuffer() and
  destroyWlSurface(), hidden functions with external linkage declared in the
  headers and defined in buffer.cpp and surface.cpp, which call the protocol
  functions.
- -Wmissing-field-initializers (pointer.cpp, touch.cpp, surface.cpp,
  xdgshell_stable.cpp, plasmawindowmanagement.cpp): the listener structs did
  not name the newer events. None of them can arrive at the versions the
  registry binds (wl_seat <= 5, wl_compositor <= 4, xdg_wm_base 1,
  org_kde_plasma_window_management <= 18), so the entries are spelled out as
  nullptr with a comment saying why; the structs were already zero-filled.
- -Wunused-parameter (plasmawindowmanagement.cpp, stackingOrderCallback):
  the no-op callback's parameters are marked [[maybe_unused]], as the
  file's other no-op callback (virtualDesktopChangedCallback) already is.
- -Woverloaded-virtual (xdgshell_p.h, reported for the base declarations):
  the XdgShellStable, XdgShellUnstableV5 and XdgShellUnstableV6 Private
  classes override some getXdgPopup() overloads and so hid the others. Each
  now has `using XdgShell::Private::getXdgPopup;`, the same way they already
  re-expose the base conversion operators. Calls go through an
  XdgShell::Private pointer, so dispatch is unchanged.

Behaviour is unchanged.

